  "findings": [
    "The selected bundle's startup witness runs only on the production worker handshake, so this repeat must run in production mode, unlike the instrumented W2 runs.",
    "The selected package carries the W2 BetterBench helper but disables it; restoring it needs edits to five sources, one of them the protected controller.",
    "Production mode has no per-request native observer, so W2's C2 global counter joins are unavailable and are reported as unavailable.",
    "The canonical serving registrar rebuilds packets at admission, requires natural-stop grading and an A/B latency report; it cannot carry this packet unchanged. The proposed carrier is the campaign pattern used by operations 154-163."
  ],
  "disclosed_risks": [
    "Sampled decoding has no GPU evidence on the selected bundle: operation 232's menu and startup probes are greedy.",
    "The native CPU proof reproduced the embedded NumPy receipt on 7 November. The actual serving launch still checks it before loading weights.",
    "BetterBench has no answer-quality oracle; operation 232's 60/60 greedy grades remain separate evidence.",
    "Production mode cannot prove per-request sampled-selector coverage on both ranks; native request and C2 joins remain unavailable.",
    "Both starts reuse port 18088 sequentially; this assumption is untested.",
    "Readout evaluate() was not tested end to end on a BetterBench-shaped operation root; the native fixture reused rebased physical-bf16 worker evidence for both starts.",
    "The client bounds prompt plus output plus reserve to 32768 tokens; server context is 131040.",
    "On failure, independent result review must authenticate protected closeout and observer/scope-absence release evidence even if finish labels release VERIFIED."
  ],
  "interpretation_rule": [
    "Report each start separately, then their mean and relative difference; two starts establish observed repeatability, not a resolved effect size.",
    "Compare with W2 descriptively only. Runtime, instrumentation, power cap, server context and sampled generated work all differ; no causal attribution to the three members and no pooling with operation 232's greedy score.",
    "A start counts only with 53/53 complete journal records, verified independent release and 235 W configured-cap readbacks on both cards before and after the caller. Otherwise the run is incomplete; partial data is retained and there is no retry."
  ],
